design:
Ids are preserved: one namespace AND one source per existing registry, both reusing registry.id. Every existing registry_id value stays valid as both namespace_id and source_id.

  INSERT INTO namespace (id, name, owner_id, visibility, ...) SELECT id, name, owner_id, visibility, ... FROM registry;
  INSERT INTO source (id, namespace_id, kind, name, ...) SELECT id, id, 'oci_registry', name, ... FROM registry;
  ALTER TABLE registry ADD CONSTRAINT fk_registry_source FOREIGN KEY (id) REFERENCES source(id) ON DELETE CASCADE;
  ALTER TABLE registry DROP COLUMN name, DROP COLUMN owner_id, DROP COLUMN visibility;

FK repointing:
  sbom              registry_id -> namespace_id (FK namespace); add source_id (FK source), same backfill value
  artifact_registry -> artifact_namespace, col -> namespace_id
  *_rollup          registry_id -> namespace_id
  scan_jobs         UNCHANGED -- only OCI sources get scanned

Visibility functions rewritten against namespace: sbom_visible(ns_id,...), artifact_visible(...), and visible_registry_ids -> visible_namespace_ids preserving the set-returning shape and the rationale comment from 00052.

description:
Per-enricher workers need to claim only their own jobs. Currently enrichment_jobs has one row per SBOM and ClaimNextEnrichmentJob uses SKIP LOCKED with no enricher filter — if two per-enricher workers compete, only one processes each SBOM. Adding enricher_name gives each worker its own independent queue.

